hx-sandbox
Part of hypotaxis.

This crate contains material derived from OpenAI Codex
(https://github.com/openai/codex, commit fecf5cc672538029b3b1adc00204a78e416a19a3),
Copyright 2025 OpenAI, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The licence text is in
LICENSE-APACHE. Each derived file carries a header that says what was taken and what changed.

Derived files:

  src/platform/linux/seccomp.rs
    From codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/seccomp.rs. Taken: the deny-list approach to
    socket()/socketpair() domains, the x32 syscall-number aliases on x86_64, and the list of
    syscalls that get around socket-family rules or the sandbox (io_uring, ptrace,
    process_vm_*). Changed: the filter is built from a three-mode enum (off, loopback, open)
    instead of Codex's proxy-routing modes; Unix socket path access (connect, bind, listen,
    datagram sockets) is closed when the network is off; the always-denied list is larger;
    the code is rewritten against this crate's types.

  src/seatbelt/base.sbpl
    From codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_base_policy.sbpl. Changed: removed the
    pseudo-terminal rules and the PyTorch/OpenMP shared-memory rule.

  src/seatbelt/platform.sbpl
    From codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_read_only_platform_defaults.sbpl. Changed: dropped
    the broad reads of /etc, /Library/Preferences, /opt/homebrew/lib and /usr/local/lib,
    the master.passwd literal, terminal rules and app-sandbox extension rules; added
    file-read-metadata.

  src/seatbelt/network_on.sbpl
    From codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_network_policy.sbpl. Changed: added the
    (allow network*) rule itself and dropped the proxy hooks.

Studied but not copied: the Windows sandbox (codex-rs/windows-sandbox-rs) and the Linux
bubblewrap launcher. The Windows backend here is written from the Win32 documentation around
AppContainer and job objects; see the README for why it differs from Codex's.
